## Bevy version and features

- Bevy 0.19.1 (crates.io), `default-features = false, features = ["2d", "3d", "ui"]`

## Relevant system information

- Rust 1.95.0, Windows 11 (10.0.26200), Vulkan
- `AdapterInfo { name: "AMD Radeon(TM) Graphics", vendor: 4098, device: 5708, device_type: IntegratedGpu, driver: "AMD proprietary driver", driver_info: "22.20.44", backend: Vulkan }`

## What you did

A `PointLight` with `shadow_maps_enabled: true` renders for 30 frames. On frame 30 the same system sets `shadow_maps_enabled = false` **and** `Visibility::Hidden`. A render-world system counts `ExtractedView`s before and after. With `-- staged`, shadows go off on frame 30 and the light is hidden on frame 31 instead.

`src/main.rs`:

```rust
//! Bevy 0.19.1: hiding a shadow-casting point light in the same frame its shadows are turned
//! off leaves its six cube-face shadow views alive in the render world.
//!
//!     cargo run --bin point_shadow_leak            # hide and disable shadows together: leaks
//!     cargo run --bin point_shadow_leak -- staged  # disable shadows, hide one frame later: fine
//!
//! Prints how many `ExtractedView`s the render world has before and after.

use bevy::prelude::*;
use bevy::render::view::ExtractedView;
use bevy::render::{Render, RenderApp, RenderSystems};
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU32, Ordering};

static FRAME: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);

#[derive(Component)]
struct Lamp;

fn main() {
    let mut app = App::new();
    app.add_plugins(DefaultPlugins).add_systems(Startup, setup).add_systems(Update, drive);
    app.sub_app_mut(RenderApp).add_systems(Render, count_views.in_set(RenderSystems::Queue));
    app.run();
}

fn setup(mut commands: Commands, mut meshes: ResMut<Assets<Mesh>>, mut materials: ResMut<Assets<StandardMaterial>>) {
    let grey = materials.add(Color::srgb(0.6, 0.6, 0.6));
    commands.spawn((Mesh3d(meshes.add(Plane3d::default().mesh().size(10.0, 10.0))), MeshMaterial3d(grey.clone())));
    commands.spawn((Mesh3d(meshes.add(Cuboid::new(1.0, 1.0, 1.0))), MeshMaterial3d(grey), Transform::from_xyz(1.0, 0.5, 0.0)));
    commands.spawn((PointLight { shadow_maps_enabled: true, range: 10.0, ..default() }, Transform::from_xyz(0.0, 2.0, 0.0), Lamp));
    commands.spawn((Camera3d::default(), Transform::from_xyz(0.0, 6.0, 8.0).looking_at(Vec3::ZERO, Vec3::Y)));
}

fn drive(mut lamp: Query<(&mut PointLight, &mut Visibility), With<Lamp>>, mut exit: MessageWriter<AppExit>) {
    let frame = FRAME.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed) + 1;
    let staged = std::env::args().any(|a| a == "staged");
    let Ok((mut light, mut vis)) = lamp.single_mut() else { return };
    if frame == 30 {
        light.shadow_maps_enabled = false;
        if !staged {
            *vis = Visibility::Hidden;
        }
    }
    if frame == 31 && staged {
        *vis = Visibility::Hidden;
    }
    if frame == 90 {
        exit.write(AppExit::Success);
    }
}

fn count_views(views: Query<&ExtractedView>) {
    let frame = FRAME.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
    if frame == 29 || frame == 60 || frame == 89 {
        println!("frame {frame}: {} extracted views in the render world", views.iter().count());
    }
}
```

## What went wrong

```
$ cargo run --release
frame 29: 8 extracted views in the render world
frame 60: 8 extracted views in the render world
frame 89: 8 extracted views in the render world

$ cargo run --release -- staged
frame 29: 8 extracted views in the render world
frame 60: 2 extracted views in the render world
frame 89: 2 extracted views in the render world
```

Hiding the light while (or in the same frame as) turning its shadows off leaves its six cube-face shadow views alive, and they keep being rendered every frame. In our game scene that was a permanent 2.8 ms a frame on an integrated GPU after the light was gone (each point/spot shadow view runs a full Core3d schedule, see #25576).

I expected the six views to be despawned once the light no longer casts shadows or is no longer visible, as happens in the staged case.

## Additional information

- From reading the 0.19.1 source: in `bevy_pbr/src/render/light.rs`, `prepare_lights` despawns a point light's view entities in `if !light.shadow_maps_enabled { despawn_entities(...) }`, but that loop only visits lights extracted this frame (`point_light_entities`). A light that stops being extracted while it still owns view entities never reaches the branch, so the views stay in the retained render world. Despawning the light entity outright may leak the same way (not tested).
- Workaround: turn shadows off for one frame while the light is still visible, then hide it.
